Subject: src/common/sysdefs.h: on OpenVMS, exit through vms_exit()

With _POSIX_EXIT the VSI C RTL gives every exit code a success severity,
so to DCL a failed xz run looked successful and ON ERROR never fired.
Route exit() (tuklib_exit() and the direct calls in xzdec and lzmainfo) to
vms_exit() (vms/vms_exit.c), which gives DCL an error severity for exit
status 1 and a warning for 2, and keeps the POSIX status under a GNV
shell.  liblzma does not call exit().

--- a/src/common/sysdefs.h	2026-10-05 11:03:46.567767123 +0100
+++ b/src/common/sysdefs.h	2026-10-05 11:03:46.590607186 +0100
@@ -226,4 +226,14 @@
 #	define FALLTHROUGH ((void)0)
 #endif
 
+#if defined(__VMS) && !defined(VMS_EXIT_IMPLEMENTATION)
+// OpenVMS: with _POSIX_EXIT the C RTL gives every exit code a success
+// severity, so to DCL a failed run looked successful.  vms_exit()
+// (vms/vms_exit.c) gives DCL an error severity for 1 and a warning for 2,
+// and keeps the POSIX status under a GNV shell.
+#	undef exit
+#	define exit vms_exit
+extern void vms_exit(int status);
+#endif
+
 #endif
